// Title: New DNS ServerLevelPluginDll Installed
// Sigma ID: e61e8a88-59a9-451c-874e-70fcc9740d67
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2017-05-08 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, stealth, defense-impairment, T1574.001, T1112
// Description: Detects the installation of a DNS plugin DLL via ServerLevelPluginDll parameter in registry,
//   which can be used to execute code in context of the DNS server (restart required)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://medium.com/@esnesenon/feature-not-bug-dnsadmin-to-dc-compromise-in-one-line-a0f779b8dc83
//   - https://blog.3or.de/hunting-dns-server-level-plugin-dll-injection.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_dns_server_level_plugin_dll.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\services\\DNS\\Parameters\\ServerLevelPluginDll"
